// A load plan with limits. An inequality is a law too. The world finds the
// limits that follow from the laws: here, how many crates fit.

#Truck: #Phenomenon & {
    crates:     %count & >=1
    crate_mass: %mass
    pallet:     %mass
    load:       %mass
    capacity:   %mass
    total: .load == .crates * .crate_mass + .pallet
    limit: .load <= .capacity
}

// How many crates of 12.5 kg fit on a truck for 1000 kg, with a pallet of 25 kg?
van: #Truck & { crate_mass: 12.5kg, pallet: 25kg, capacity: 1000kg }

// The other direction: 40 crates must fit. How heavy can one crate be?
order: #Truck & { crates: 40, pallet: 25kg, capacity: 1000kg }
